          "kicker": "Stuart effect",
          "heading": "BBC credits Will Stuart's Achilles comeback with reviving England's attacking swagger",
          "body": "BBC Sport's Mike Henson ties England's revival to Will Stuart, the England and British and Irish Lions star who missed the start of the year with a ruptured Achilles tendon. Without him England endured a terrible Six Nations and five straight defeats. Since his return they have scored 20 tries against Australia and Japan and rank top of the Nations Championship for points scored and entries into the opposition 22. New Zealand arrive at Twickenham on Saturday stung by last weekend's 35-28 defeat to Wales."
        },
