      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Referee row",
          "heading": "Fabien Galthié defends referees after Rassie Erasmus's six-match ban for match-fixing claim",
          "body": "France head coach Fabien Galthié said on Thursday coaches have a duty to protect referees. He did so without naming Springbok coach Rassie Erasmus, banned for six matches for suggesting officials' failure to punish knee-drop tackles in France's 21-19 win in Paris amounted to “manipulation” or “match-fixing”. “If I don't take care with the words I use when discussing refereeing, I can cause harm to rugby, the supporters and our opponents,” he said. Since 2020, he added, he has backed officials whatever the result, airing disagreements only with those who manage the laws."
        },
