          "heading": "Harry Wilson says dry Cardiff roof gives Wallabies licence to attack",
          "body": "Wallabies captain Harry Wilson expects Cardiff's Principality Stadium roof to free the attack that stalled in Murrayfield's drizzle. By his account, the 12-15 loss to Scotland was little more than box kicks and chasing scraps. For Saturday's test against Wales, \"dry conditions, we really have a licence to back our game,\" he said, name-checking Tom Hooper and Carlo Tizzano, promoted to the starting pack alongside a front row lifted from the bench. Wales arrive buoyed by last weekend's 35-28 win over the All Blacks."
